      "message": "[From Jetski review] `ArgsLike\u003c\u0027v\u003e` implements `Freeze`, but `ArgsList\u003c\u0027v\u003e` is missing `#[derive(Freeze, Trace)]` (and `ArgsLike\u003c\u0027v\u003e` is also missing `Trace`). Without `Freeze` on `ArgsList`, there is currently no way to freeze an `ArgsList` containing unfrozen `ArgsLike::Args` into `ArgsLike::FrozenArgs` before calling `expand()`.\n\nAlso, per the crate encapsulation guidelines in `AGENTS.md`, can `ArgsLike` (and `mod args_list` in `lib.rs`) be `pub(crate)` instead of `pub`? That would also prevent external callers from constructing `ArgsLike::FrozenArgs(args, upto)` with an out-of-bounds `upto`.",
